      <li>Shanghai ≈47m TEU versus Ningbo-Zhoushan ≈35m TEU is a 12m TEU gap that favours Shanghai for dense schedule-sensitive flows.</li>
      <li>Ningbo-Zhoushan counters with world #1 total cargo tonnage and ≈18 m draft versus Shanghai’s ≈15.5 m at Yangshan.</li>
      <li>Zhejiang small commodities, hardware, bulk and ultra-large-vessel cargo fit Ningbo-Zhoushan; YRD electronics, machinery and time-sensitive project cargo fit Shanghai.</li>
