    <p><strong>Position:</strong> I would not send time-sensitive YRD project cargo to Ningbo-Zhoushan to chase a marginal origin saving, because Shanghai’s profile gives it the denser direct Gulf schedule. For Zhejiang-origin or heavy/deep-draft cargo, I would not default to Shanghai either — the inland haul and ≈18 m draft make Ningbo-Zhoushan the structurally better fit.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Shanghai throughput minus Ningbo-Zhoushan throughput is 47 − 35 = 12m TEU, but that only measures container scale, not your inland leg.</li>
      <li>Draft gap is 18 − 15.5 = 2.5 m, which can decide vessel-size and heavy-cargo feasibility.</li>
      <li>The port profiles publish no rate or transit figures, so the final choice must follow a live factory-to-terminal quote and a confirmed direct/transshipped sailing.</li>
